ed little money and has no outside support.\n\nRecent polls from UNH and Braun Research, taken in late September, show Balint leading by margins ranging from 15 to 36 points, with the most recent live-caller surveys around 30 points. The Cook Political Report called the race an easy incumbent win, and prediction markets price her chances near 98 percent. Independent candidates on the ballot appear to lack traction. Everything points to a comfortable Balint reelection.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9976, "margin": 26.51}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9992, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9998, "margin": 33.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9994, "margin": 32.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9993, "margin": 30.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.999, "margin": 26.0}]}